# The raw curated-art source dump (~1.4GB, thousands of files) - only
# the small, resized subset this project actually uses ever gets
# committed, under launcher/platform_icons/ and launcher/
# platform_wallpapers/ (see launcher/platform_art.py) - not this
# folder itself.
/images-for-use/
# Runtime log output from GameGrubber - never source, never worth
# committing. gamegrubber/ itself is gone from this repo entirely now -
# a real, separately-installed module (see packaging/module_registry.py)
# fetched into /userdata/modules_repo, not a plain sibling directory
# here - but its own runtime config dir (RGSX_CONFIG_DIR, still set to
# COSMOS_ROOT/data/gamegrubber - see gamegrubber/cosmos_bridge.py's own
# docstring) still lands under this checkout's data/ directory.
/data/gamegrubber/logs/
# "One emulator, every core and asset" (RetroArch) means the full real
# buildbot set - well over a gigabyte, and would hit GitHub's hard
# 100MB-per-file push limit repeatedly (mame_libretro.so alone is
# ~400MB). Fetched at deploy time instead - see emulators/cores.py and
# emulators/assets.py. Only the from-source retroarch binary itself
# stays committed.
/emulators/bin/cores/
/emulators/bin/assets/
/emulators/bin/autoconfig/
/emulators/bin/cheats/
/emulators/bin/database/
/emulators/bin/info/
/emulators/bin/overlays/
/emulators/bin/shaders/
# Same story for the indie game-engine runtimes (NW.js/LÖVE/Ren'Py/
# TIC-80/AGS) - real prebuilt third-party binaries, fetched at deploy
# time (emulators/engines.py), never committed.
/emulators/bin/engines/
# Same story again for the Electron runtime webshell/main.js runs on
# (replaced Brave - see webshell/electron_runtime.py) - a real
# unmodified upstream binary release, fetched at deploy time, not
# committed. First-party app code alongside it (main.js, package.json,
# etc.) is NOT excluded, only this one fetched directory.
/webshell/electron/
# mkxp-z's own generated per-launch game config (see mkxp_config.py) -
# the bundled mkxp-z.x86_64 binary/lib64/stdlib next to it ARE
# committed (built from source, no prebuilt release exists), but this
# one file is regenerated fresh before every RPG Maker XP/VX/VXAce
# launch, never static.
/emulators/bin/mkxpz/mkxp.json
# launcher/avatar3d_previewer.py's own saved test combos - real
# throwaway dev-session data (F5 in that tool), never a real profile's
# actual picture (those live in a profile's own picture_traits.json,
# under /userdata, never in the git tree at all).
/launcher/avatar3d_previewer_seeds.json
# launcher/avatar3d_mega_showcase.py's own rendered grid PNGs - same
# "throwaway dev-session output, regenerate on demand" reasoning.
/launcher/avatar3d_mega_showcase_output/
